# =============================================================================
# Bharat Connect (BBPS) SDK — Gherkin Feature File
# Embedded bill payment experience for partner banks
# Scope: SDK init | Logo rules | Home | Fetch & Pay | Payment result | My Billers |
#        Payments | Complaints | Non-functional
# Version: v1.0 | Author: Product Team
# Note: "Screen" means a generic SDK screen. Host banks may style colours, fonts
#       and navigation, but NOT the Bharat Connect / B Assured brand assets.
# =============================================================================

# References:
#   - NPCI Bharat Connect Brand Guidelines (logo, B Assured, sonic branding, receipts)
#   - Reference implementation screens (Home, My Billers, Payments, Complaints)
#
# Brand specification used in this file (from NPCI guidelines):
#   Stage 1 : "B" mnemonic at the entry point of the bill payment section (host app)
#   Stage 2 : Bharat Connect horizontal logo on Selection of Biller, Bill Fetch, Bill Payment,
#             Transaction Status History and Complaint Management screens
#             - top right-hand corner, minimum height 20 px
#   Stage 3 : B Assured logo on payment confirmation page and receipt (digital + physical)
#             - minimum height 30 px, white background on confirmation page
#             - online receipt: top left | paper receipt: top right (30 mm)
#   Sonic   : designated audio clip played simultaneously with B Assured on the
#             "Payment Successful" screen
#   Receipt : must show B-Connect Txn ID and Consumer Convenience Fee (CCF)
#   Layout  : designs referenced at 320 px (mobile) and 1024 px (web)


# =============================================================================
# FEATURE 1: SDK initialisation, configuration and host integration
# =============================================================================

Feature: SDK initialisation, configuration and host integration
  As a partner bank embedding the Bharat Connect SDK
  I want the SDK to initialise correctly, accept my configuration and integrate cleanly with my host application
  So that my customers can use bill payment securely inside my app while the NPCI brand assets stay protected

  Background:
    Given the host application has integrated the Bharat Connect SDK
    And the SDK has been initialised with a valid partner configuration
    And the SDK has received a valid authenticated customer session from the host application

  Scenario: SDK initialises successfully with valid configuration
    Given the host provides partner ID, environment, customer identifier and session token
    When the host application launches the Bharat Connect SDK
    Then the SDK should open the Home module
    And the SDK should not expose any customer data to the host beyond the defined callbacks

  Scenario Outline: SDK refuses to start with invalid configuration
    Given the host provides "<invalid_input>"
    When the host application launches the Bharat Connect SDK
    Then the SDK should not open any screen
    And the SDK should return error code "<error_code>" to the host callback

    Examples:
      | invalid_input           | error_code           |
      | missing partner ID      | ERR_INVALID_PARTNER  |
      | expired session token   | ERR_SESSION_EXPIRED  |
      | unsupported environment | ERR_INVALID_ENV      |
      | missing customer ID     | ERR_INVALID_CUSTOMER |

  Scenario: Host bank applies its own theme without altering brand assets
    Given the host supplies a theme with primary colour, font family and bank logo
    When the SDK renders any screen
    Then buttons, headers and text should use the host theme
    And the host bank logo should be displayed in the header area
    And the Bharat Connect logo should be rendered from the SDK bundled asset
    And the Bharat Connect logo should not be recolored, stretched, cropped, rotated or re-typeset

  Scenario: Host cannot override Bharat Connect or B Assured assets
    Given the host supplies a custom image as the Bharat Connect logo
    When the SDK is initialised
    Then the SDK should ignore the custom image
    And the SDK should continue to use the official Bharat Connect and B Assured assets

  Scenario Outline: SDK notifies the host about key events
    When the "<event>" occurs inside the SDK
    Then the SDK should invoke the host callback "<callback>" with the event payload

    Examples:
      | event                  | callback          |
      | payment completed      | onPaymentResult   |
      | biller added           | onBillerAdded     |
      | biller deleted         | onBillerDeleted   |
      | complaint raised       | onComplaintRaised |
      | customer exits the SDK | onSDKClosed       |
      | session expired        | onSessionExpired  |

  Scenario: Customer session expires while using the SDK
    Given the customer is on any SDK screen
    When the host session token expires
    Then the SDK should show a "Session expired" message
    And the SDK should call "onSessionExpired" so the host can re-authenticate
    And the SDK should not allow further actions until a new token is provided

  Scenario Outline: Host entry point uses the B mnemonic (Stage 1)
    Given the host application shows a bill payment entry on its "<surface>"
    When the entry tile or menu item is rendered
    Then it should display the B mnemonic from the SDK brand asset kit
    And the label should be one of "Bill Payments", "Pay Bills" or "Bill Pay"
    And the B mnemonic should be prominent and commensurate with other entries in the host design

    Examples:
      | surface                         |
      | mobile app home grid            |
      | mobile app with dark background |
      | website dropdown menu           |
      | net-banking landing page        |

  Scenario Outline: SDK renders correctly on supported form factors
    Given the SDK is launched on a "<device>" with viewport width "<width>"
    When any SDK screen is displayed
    Then the layout should adapt without horizontal scrolling
    And all primary actions should remain visible and tappable

    Examples:
      | device        | width   |
      | mobile        | 320 px  |
      | tablet        | 768 px  |
      | web / desktop | 1024 px |


# =============================================================================
# FEATURE 2: Bharat Connect logo (Stage 2) rendering rules across SDK screens
# =============================================================================

Feature: Bharat Connect logo (Stage 2) rendering rules across SDK screens
  As a partner bank embedding the Bharat Connect SDK
  I want the Bharat Connect logo to be displayed consistently on the mandated screens
  So that my integration stays compliant with the NPCI Bharat Connect brand guidelines

  Background:
    Given the host application has integrated the Bharat Connect SDK
    And the SDK has been initialised with a valid partner configuration
    And the SDK has received a valid authenticated customer session from the host application

  Scenario Outline: Bharat Connect logo is shown on mandatory screens
    When the customer opens the "<screen>" screen
    Then the Bharat Connect horizontal logo should be displayed
    And the logo should be positioned in the top right-hand corner
    And the logo should be clearly visible against the header background

    Examples:
      | screen                     |
      | Selection of Biller        |
      | Bill Fetch                 |
      | Bill Payment               |
      | Transaction Status History |
      | Raise Complaint            |
      | Complaint Status           |

  Scenario Outline: Bharat Connect logo respects minimum size
    Given the SDK is rendered on "<device>"
    When the Bharat Connect logo is displayed
    Then its rendered height should be at least 20 px
    And its aspect ratio should be preserved

    Examples:
      | device |
      | mobile |
      | tablet |
      | web    |

  Scenario: Logo remains visible when host header is small
    Given the host header area is shorter than the minimum logo size
    When the SDK renders a screen with the Bharat Connect logo
    Then the SDK should enlarge the header or reposition the logo so the 20 px minimum is met
    And the logo should never be hidden, clipped or overlapped by other elements

  Scenario: Vertical logo not permitted by host design guidelines
    Given the host design guidelines do not allow the vertical logo
    When the SDK renders a Stage 2 screen
    Then the SDK should use the Bharat Connect horizontal logo

  Scenario: Logo is shown in the correct variant on dark backgrounds
    Given the host uses a dark header background
    When the SDK renders the Bharat Connect logo
    Then the SDK should use the approved dark-background variant with sufficient contrast


# =============================================================================
# FEATURE 3: Home module - biller categories, registered billers and search
# =============================================================================

Feature: Home module - biller categories, registered billers and search
  As a customer using the Bharat Connect SDK
  I want to see biller categories, my registered billers and a search option on the Home screen
  So that I can quickly find a biller and start paying my bill

  Background:
    Given the host application has integrated the Bharat Connect SDK
    And the SDK has been initialised with a valid partner configuration
    And the SDK has received a valid authenticated customer session from the host application

  Scenario: Home screen displays navigation, categories and registered billers
    When the customer opens the Home module
    Then the SDK should display the navigation to "Home", "My Billers", "Payments" and "Complaints"
    And the SDK should display an "Add Biller" button
    And the SDK should display a search box for billers
    And the SDK should display the list of biller categories as tiles with icons
    And the Bharat Connect logo should be visible in the top right-hand corner

  Scenario: Registered billers are listed on Home with pending bills
    Given the customer has registered billers
    When the Home screen loads
    Then the SDK should list each registered biller with serial number, biller name, authenticator and pending bill amount
    And each row should have a "Fetch" action
    And the list should be paginated with a rows-per-page selector

  Scenario: Home screen when the customer has no registered billers
    Given the customer has no registered billers
    When the Home screen loads
    Then the SDK should show an empty state with a message to add a biller
    And the category tiles should still be displayed

  Scenario Outline: Biller categories are displayed as defined by the Bharat Connect biller master
    When the Home screen loads
    Then the category "<category>" should be available as a tile

    Examples:
      | category           |
      | Electricity        |
      | Water              |
      | Gas                |
      | Mobile Postpaid    |
      | Mobile Prepaid     |
      | DTH                |
      | Broadband Postpaid |
      | Landline Postpaid  |
      | Credit Card        |
      | Loan Repayment     |
      | Insurance          |
      | FASTag             |
      | Municipal Taxes    |
      | Education Fees     |

  Scenario: Categories are driven by the central biller master
    Given a new biller category is enabled in the biller master
    When the Home screen loads
    Then the new category should appear without requiring an SDK upgrade

  Scenario: Search a biller from the Home screen
    Given the customer is on the Home screen
    When the customer types "air" in the biller search box
    Then the SDK should show only billers whose names contain "air"
    And the search should be case-insensitive

  Scenario: Search returns no result
    When the customer searches for a biller name that does not exist
    Then the SDK should show a "No billers found" message

  Scenario: Selecting a category opens biller selection (Stage 2)
    When the customer taps the "Credit Card" category tile
    Then the SDK should open the Selection of Biller screen
    And the screen title should show "Credit Card"
    And the Bharat Connect logo should be displayed in the top right-hand corner
    And a back control should return the customer to Home

  Scenario: Biller dropdown supports search within a category
    Given the customer is on the Selection of Biller screen for "Credit Card"
    When the customer opens the biller dropdown and types a biller name
    Then the dropdown should filter to matching billers
    And each biller should show its name and logo

  Scenario: Category has no billers available
    Given a category has no active billers
    When the customer opens that category
    Then the SDK should show "No billers available for this category"


# =============================================================================
# FEATURE 4: Fetch bill and pay flow (Selection of Biller, Bill Fetch, Bill Payment)
# =============================================================================

Feature: Fetch bill and pay flow (Selection of Biller, Bill Fetch, Bill Payment)
  As a customer using the Bharat Connect SDK
  I want to fetch my bill, review it and pay it from my preferred account
  So that I can complete my bill payment securely and without errors

  Background:
    Given the host application has integrated the Bharat Connect SDK
    And the SDK has been initialised with a valid partner configuration
    And the SDK has received a valid authenticated customer session from the host application

  Scenario: Customer parameter form is generated from biller metadata
    Given the customer has selected a biller
    When the customer parameter screen loads
    Then the SDK should render input fields exactly as defined in the biller MDM
    And mandatory fields should be marked as required
    And each field should apply the data type, length and regex validation from the MDM
    And the Bharat Connect logo should be displayed in the top right-hand corner

  Scenario: Consent note is displayed before fetching
    Given the customer is on the customer parameter screen
    Then the SDK should display a consent note stating that proceeding registers the biller and authorises fetching of current and future bills
    And the note should state that consent can be withdrawn by deleting the biller from My Billers

  Scenario: Successful bill fetch
    Given the customer has entered valid customer parameters
    When the customer taps "Fetch"
    Then the SDK should call the Bharat Connect fetch request
    And the SDK should show a bill details view with bill amount, due date, customer name and bill number
    And the view should provide "Cancel" and "Confirm & Pay" actions
    And the Bharat Connect logo should be displayed in the top right-hand corner

  Scenario Outline: Validation errors on customer parameters
    Given the customer is on the customer parameter screen
    When the customer enters "<input>" in the field "<field>"
    And the customer taps "Fetch"
    Then the SDK should show the inline error "<message>"
    And no fetch request should be sent

    Examples:
      | field                 | input | message                       |
      | Registered Mobile No  |       | This field is required        |
      | Registered Mobile No  | 12345 | Enter a valid 10 digit number |
      | Last 4 digits of card | 12    | Enter exactly 4 digits        |
      | Last 4 digits of card | abcd  | Only digits are allowed       |

  Scenario: Bill fetch returns no pending bill
    Given the biller returns "no dues"
    When the customer taps "Fetch"
    Then the SDK should show "No pending bill found"
    And the SDK should not display the "Confirm & Pay" action

  Scenario: Biller does not support fetch (quick pay / instapay)
    Given the selected biller supports pay-without-fetch
    When the customer enters the payment amount directly
    Then the SDK should skip the bill details view
    And proceed to the payment confirmation view

  Scenario Outline: Bill fetch failures are handled gracefully
    Given the customer taps "Fetch"
    When the fetch fails with "<reason>"
    Then the SDK should show the message "<message>"
    And the customer should be able to retry or go back

    Examples:
      | reason                | message                                           |
      | biller unavailable    | Biller is currently unavailable. Try again later. |
      | invalid customer data | Details entered are incorrect. Please re-check.   |
      | network timeout       | Request timed out. Please try again.              |

  Scenario: Fetch for a registered biller directly from Home
    Given the customer has a registered biller on the Home screen
    When the customer taps "Fetch" against that biller
    Then the SDK should show the bill details view without asking for customer parameters again
    And the customer should be able to proceed with "Confirm & Pay"

  Scenario: Payment configuration view
    Given the customer has confirmed the fetched bill
    When the SDK shows the payment view
    Then the SDK should display biller name, "When to pay", payment amount, Consumer Convenience Fee and payment method
    And the total payable amount should include the CCF and applicable taxes
    And the Bharat Connect logo should be displayed in the top right-hand corner

  Scenario Outline: Payment amount rules
    Given the fetched bill amount is 1000
    And the biller "<amount_rule>"
    When the customer enters payment amount "<entered>"
    Then the SDK should "<result>"

    Examples:
      | amount_rule                      | entered | result                              |
      | allows only exact payment        | 1000    | accept the amount                   |
      | allows only exact payment        | 500     | reject with "Exact amount required" |
      | allows partial payment (min 200) | 500     | accept the amount                   |
      | allows partial payment (min 200) | 100     | reject with "Below minimum amount"  |
      | allows partial payment (min 200) | 1500    | reject with "Above bill amount"     |
      | allows any amount                | 2000    | accept the amount                   |

  Scenario: Customer selects the source account / payment method
    Given the host provides the customer's eligible payment methods
    When the customer opens the payment method list
    Then the SDK should list masked accounts with available balance if shared by the host
    And the customer should be able to select one

  Scenario: Insufficient balance
    Given the selected account balance is lower than the total payable amount
    When the customer taps "Confirm & Pay"
    Then the SDK should show "Insufficient balance"
    And the payment should not be initiated

  Scenario: Customer authorises the payment with OTP
    Given the customer has tapped "Confirm & Pay"
    When the SDK or host triggers the authentication step
    Then an OTP verification view should show the masked mobile number
    And the view should provide a 6 digit OTP input, "Cancel", "Submit" and a resend timer

  Scenario Outline: OTP verification outcomes
    Given the OTP verification view is displayed
    When the customer "<action>"
    Then the SDK should "<result>"

    Examples:
      | action                     | result                                    |
      | enters the correct OTP     | submit the payment                        |
      | enters a wrong OTP         | show "Invalid OTP" and allow retry        |
      | enters a wrong OTP 3 times | block further attempts and close the view |
      | lets the OTP expire        | enable "Resend OTP" and clear the input   |
      | taps "Cancel"              | close the view and return to payment view |

  Scenario: Resend OTP is available only after the timer ends
    Given the OTP verification view is displayed
    Then the "Resend OTP" action should be disabled until the countdown completes
    When the countdown completes
    Then the "Resend OTP" action should be enabled

  Scenario: Duplicate payment is prevented
    Given the customer has already submitted a payment for the same bill
    When the customer taps "Confirm & Pay" again
    Then the SDK should disable repeated submission while a request is in progress
    And the SDK should show a message about the existing payment in progress

  Scenario: Customer saves the biller during payment
    Given the customer is on the payment view
    When the customer selects the "Save to My Billers" option and completes the payment
    Then the biller should be added to My Billers

  Scenario Outline: Payment timing options
    Given the customer is on the payment view
    When the customer selects "When to pay" as "<timing>"
    Then the SDK should "<behaviour>"

    Examples:
      | timing    | behaviour                                            |
      | Pay Now   | process the payment immediately after authentication |
      | Pay Later | ask for a date and schedule the payment              |


# =============================================================================
# FEATURE 5: Payment result - Stage 3 B Assured, sonic branding and receipts
# =============================================================================

Feature: Payment result - Stage 3 B Assured, sonic branding and receipts
  As a customer who has attempted a bill payment
  I want a clear result screen with the right brand marks and a receipt
  So that I know the outcome of my payment and have proof of it

  Background:
    Given the host application has integrated the Bharat Connect SDK
    And the SDK has been initialised with a valid partner configuration
    And the SDK has received a valid authenticated customer session from the host application

  Scenario: Successful payment confirmation shows B Assured logo
    Given the payment is processed successfully
    When the confirmation screen is displayed
    Then the SDK should show a "Payment Successful" status
    And the B Assured logo should be displayed on a white background
    And the B Assured logo height should be at least 30 px
    And the SDK should show payment amount, CCF, total amount, source reference number, B-Connect Txn ID, transaction reference number, transaction date and time, payment status, payment channel, payment method, biller status, biller ID, approval reference number and subscriber number

  Scenario: Sonic branding plays with B Assured on success
    Given the payment is successful
    When the B Assured logo is displayed on the confirmation screen
    Then the SDK should play the designated Bharat Connect sonic audio clip simultaneously
    And the audio clip should be the unmodified file supplied by NPCI
    And the tone, tempo and audio characteristics should be identical on every platform and device

  Scenario Outline: Sonic branding handling for device audio states
    Given the payment is successful
    And the device is in "<audio_state>"
    When the confirmation screen is displayed
    Then the SDK should "<behaviour>"

    Examples:
      | audio_state               | behaviour                                       |
      | normal volume             | play the sonic clip once                        |
      | silent / muted            | not force volume and still display B Assured    |
      | another app playing audio | briefly duck other audio and play the clip once |
      | screen re-rendered        | not replay the clip                             |

  Scenario: Sonic clip fails to load
    Given the payment is successful
    And the sonic audio asset cannot be loaded
    When the confirmation screen is displayed
    Then the SDK should still display the confirmation and the B Assured logo
    And the SDK should log the audio failure without showing an error to the customer

  Scenario Outline: B Assured and sonic branding are shown only for successful payments
    Given the payment outcome is "<outcome>"
    When the result screen is displayed
    Then the B Assured logo should "<logo_behaviour>"
    And the sonic clip should "<sonic_behaviour>"

    Examples:
      | outcome | logo_behaviour   | sonic_behaviour |
      | success | be displayed     | be played       |
      | failed  | not be displayed | not be played   |
      | pending | not be displayed | not be played   |

  Scenario: Failed payment screen
    Given the payment fails
    When the result screen is displayed
    Then the SDK should show "Bill Payment Failed" with a failure indicator
    And the SDK should show the payment details and failure status
    And the SDK should offer "Cancel" and "Download" actions
    And the customer should be able to retry the payment

  Scenario: Pending payment screen
    Given the payment status is not yet known
    When the result screen is displayed
    Then the SDK should show "Bill Payment Pending" with a pending indicator
    And the SDK should tell the customer the status will be updated shortly
    And the SDK should show the reference numbers needed to track the transaction

  Scenario Outline: Pending payment is reconciled
    Given a payment is in "Pending" status
    When the final status is "<final_status>"
    Then the transaction history should show status "<final_status>"
    And the SDK should call "onPaymentResult" with "<final_status>"

    Examples:
      | final_status |
      | Success      |
      | Failed       |

  Scenario: Network is lost after the payment request is submitted
    Given the customer submitted a payment
    When the network connection is lost before a response is received
    Then the SDK should not show "Failed"
    And the SDK should show "Payment status being confirmed"
    And the SDK should check the status using the transaction reference when connectivity returns

  Scenario: Online (digital) receipt layout
    Given the payment is successful
    When the customer views or downloads the digital receipt
    Then the B Assured logo should be in the top left-hand corner of the receipt
    And the receipt should show the title "Bharat Connect - Payment Confirmation"
    And the receipt should show the B-Connect Txn ID
    And the receipt should show the Consumer Convenience Fee (CCF), even if the value is 0.00
    And the receipt should show biller name, bill number, bill date, due date, bill amount, total amount, payment mode, payment channel, transaction date and time and status

  Scenario: Paper (physical) receipt layout
    Given the host prints a receipt through a retail or assisted channel
    When the SDK provides the printable receipt
    Then the B Assured logo should be in the top right-hand corner
    And the logo should be 30 mm in height on an A4 (210 mm) page
    And the receipt should show the B-Connect Txn ID and the Consumer Convenience Fee (CCF)

  Scenario Outline: Mandatory fields on every receipt
    Given a receipt is generated in "<format>" format
    Then the receipt should contain "<mandatory_field>"

    Examples:
      | format  | mandatory_field          |
      | digital | B-Connect Txn ID         |
      | digital | Consumer Convenience Fee |
      | digital | B Assured logo           |
      | paper   | B-Connect Txn ID         |
      | paper   | Consumer Convenience Fee |
      | paper   | B Assured logo           |

  Scenario: Receipt download and share
    Given the customer is on a result screen or a transaction detail view
    When the customer taps "Download"
    Then the SDK should generate the receipt file
    And the file should be handed to the host for saving or sharing as per platform capability

  Scenario: Host support details appear on the receipt footer
    Given the host supplied support contact details in configuration
    When a receipt is generated
    Then the footer should show the host bank name, toll free number and website


# =============================================================================
# FEATURE 6: My Billers module - add, view, modify, delete, autopay
# =============================================================================

Feature: My Billers module - add, view, modify, delete, autopay
  As a customer using the Bharat Connect SDK
  I want to add, view, modify and delete my saved billers and manage autopay
  So that my repeat bill payments are quick and under my control

  Background:
    Given the host application has integrated the Bharat Connect SDK
    And the SDK has been initialised with a valid partner configuration
    And the SDK has received a valid authenticated customer session from the host application

  Scenario: My Billers list
    When the customer opens the My Billers module
    Then the SDK should list saved billers with serial number, biller name, authenticator, status, autopay toggle and an action menu
    And the SDK should display an "Add Biller" button
    And the SDK should display notes explaining biller statuses
    And the Bharat Connect logo should be displayed in the top right-hand corner

  Scenario: My Billers empty state
    Given the customer has no saved billers
    When the customer opens My Billers
    Then the SDK should display an empty state illustration with an "Add Biller" button

  Scenario Outline: Biller registration statuses
    Given a biller is saved with registration status "<status>"
    When the My Billers list is displayed
    Then the biller should show the status "<status>"
    And the SDK should "<behaviour>"

    Examples:
      | status                    | behaviour                                          |
      | Active                    | allow fetch and pay for this biller                |
      | Pending for authorization | block fetch and pay until the biller confirms      |
      | Rejected                  | show the rejection and allow only modify or delete |

  Scenario: Add biller with required details
    Given the customer is on My Billers
    When the customer taps "Add Biller"
    Then the SDK should show a form with category, biller, the biller specific parameters and a nickname
    And the form should include an "Autopay bills for this biller" toggle if the biller supports autopay
    And the consent note should be displayed

  Scenario: Biller added successfully
    Given the customer has entered valid details in the Add Biller form
    When the customer confirms the details on the review view
    Then the SDK should register the biller with Bharat Connect
    And the SDK should show "Biller Added Successfully" with nickname, biller ID, registration date, status, biller account ID, unique registration number, autopay status and payment channel
    And the customer should be able to return to Home

  Scenario: Review details before adding
    Given the customer has filled the Add Biller form
    When the customer taps "Add Biller"
    Then the SDK should show a review view with all entered values
    And the customer should confirm before the biller is registered

  Scenario: Add biller that already exists
    Given the biller with the same parameters is already saved
    When the customer tries to add it again
    Then the SDK should show "This biller is already marked as a favourite"
    And no duplicate entry should be created

  Scenario Outline: Add biller failure scenarios
    When the biller registration fails with "<reason>"
    Then the SDK should show an "Add Biller Failed" view with the message "<message>"
    And the customer should be able to retry or go back

    Examples:
      | reason             | message                                    |
      | invalid parameters | The details provided could not be verified |
      | biller unavailable | Biller is currently unavailable            |
      | rejected by biller | The biller rejected this registration      |
      | network timeout    | Request timed out. Please try again        |

  Scenario: Nickname is validated
    When the customer enters a nickname longer than the allowed length or with unsupported characters
    Then the SDK should show an inline validation error
    And the biller should not be added

  Scenario: View biller details
    Given a saved biller exists
    When the customer chooses "View Details" from the action menu
    Then the SDK should show the biller parameters, nickname and autopay status in read-only form

  Scenario: Modify biller details
    Given a saved biller exists
    When the customer chooses "Modify Details" and edits the nickname
    And the customer taps "Modify"
    Then the SDK should show the updated details for confirmation
    And on confirmation the SDK should update the biller and refresh the list

  Scenario: Biller category and biller are not editable on modify
    When the customer opens "Modify Details"
    Then the category and biller fields should not be changeable
    And only fields permitted by the biller MDM should be editable

  Scenario: Delete biller with confirmation
    Given a saved biller exists
    When the customer chooses "Delete" from the action menu
    Then the SDK should show a confirmation with nickname, biller account ID and account number
    When the customer taps "Confirm & Delete"
    Then the SDK should remove the biller and any autopay mandate linked to it
    And the SDK should show "Biller Deleted Successfully" with a "Download" option

  Scenario: Delete is cancelled
    When the customer closes the delete confirmation without confirming
    Then the biller should remain in My Billers

  Scenario Outline: Autopay toggle behaviour
    Given a saved biller "<support>" autopay
    When the customer views the autopay toggle
    Then the toggle should be "<state>"

    Examples:
      | support          | state                   |
      | supports         | enabled                 |
      | does not support | disabled with a tooltip |

  Scenario: Enable autopay on a saved biller
    Given the customer has an Active biller that supports autopay
    When the customer turns the autopay toggle on
    Then the SDK should ask the customer to authorise the mandate
    And on success the toggle should show ON

  Scenario: Disable autopay on a saved biller
    Given autopay is ON for a biller
    When the customer turns the toggle off and confirms
    Then the SDK should cancel the mandate
    And the toggle should show OFF

  Scenario: My Billers pagination
