# FEATURE 9: Non-functional, security, accessibility and compliance
# =============================================================================

Feature: Non-functional, security, accessibility and compliance
  As a partner bank embedding the Bharat Connect SDK
  I want the SDK to meet security, accessibility, language and compliance requirements
  So that the integration can be certified by NPCI and rolled out safely to customers

  Background:
    Given the host application has integrated the Bharat Connect SDK
    And the SDK has been initialised with a valid partner configuration
    And the SDK has received a valid authenticated customer session from the host application

  Scenario: Sensitive data is masked
    When the SDK displays account numbers, mobile numbers or card digits
    Then the values should be masked except for the permitted last digits

  Scenario: No sensitive data in logs or screenshots
    When the SDK logs diagnostics
    Then OTPs, PINs, full account numbers and tokens should never be written to logs
    And sensitive screens such as OTP verification should block screenshots where the platform supports it

  Scenario: All network calls are secured
    When the SDK communicates with the Bharat Connect or partner services
    Then all calls should use TLS
    And each request should carry a unique request ID for traceability

  Scenario: Idle timeout
    Given the customer has been inactive on the SDK for the host configured idle time
    When the timeout is reached
    Then the SDK should end the session and notify the host

  Scenario: No internet connectivity
    Given the device has no internet connection
    When the customer performs any action that needs the network
    Then the SDK should show "No internet connection" with a "Retry" option

  Scenario: Accessibility support
    When a customer uses a screen reader, large fonts or keyboard navigation
    Then all controls should have accessible labels
    And colour must not be the only indicator of status
    And the Bharat Connect and B Assured logos should have alternative text

  Scenario Outline: Language support
    Given the host sets the SDK language to "<language>"
    When any SDK screen is displayed
    Then all SDK text should appear in "<language>"
    But the "Bharat Connect" and "B Assured" brand marks should remain unchanged

    Examples:
      | language |
      | English  |
      | Hindi    |
      | Bengali  |

  Scenario: Brand asset kit is versioned with the SDK
    Given NPCI publishes updated brand assets or sonic audio
    When the host upgrades to the latest SDK version
    Then the SDK should ship the updated assets
    And the SDK should expose its version and brand asset version to the host

  Scenario: Brand compliance checklist for certification
    When the host submits the integration for NPCI certification
    Then the following should be verifiable:
      | check                                                                               |
      | B mnemonic present at the entry point of the bill payment section                   |
      | Bharat Connect logo on biller selection, fetch, payment, history, complaint screens |
      | Logos in the top right-hand corner with minimum 20 px height                        |
      | B Assured logo on payment confirmation and receipts only for success                |
      | B Assured minimum 30 px, white background on confirmation page                      |
      | Sonic branding played with B Assured on success screen                              |
      | B-Connect Txn ID and CCF present on every receipt                                   |
